    "description": "PUC Transmission LP is a regulated transmission development platform in Sault Ste. Marie, Ontario. The company is developing a 230 kV transmission line and transformer station intended to connect new industrial and regional loads, including Algoma Steel’s electric arc furnace project. Its operating model is asset-heavy and regulated, with cost recovery and allowed returns governed by Ontario’s utility regulatory framework rather than merchant power exposure. Public materials describe the project as approximately 10 kilometers of double-circuit line and a new 230 kV station, with commercial operation expected by the end of 2027. PUC Transmission was incorporated in 2021, and Axium acquired an 80% equity interest in 2024 while the Public Utility Commission of Sault Ste. Marie retained 20%.",
